Z||000000||Ironhorse||06-13-2000||11:22 PM||||I got a oil tube where the dipstick goes in.. The dipstick is fine but the tube is bent all out of shape.  This tube is discontinue by the dealer. *sniffle* I'm not in a real hunting mood.  I've been hunting for s*itload of parts for it and I'm pooped.  I've heard that they have universal kit for cases like this but have no idea where to start looking. I would appreaciate any help or information. Thanks.   P.S. would something like a bretta or caliver 2.8 oil dipstick tube work on this?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Phaeton||06-14-2000||01:34 AM||||A 2.8 set from a S10 may be a bolt in, but will give a good reading regardless, as long as the tube is seated.<P>The stick and the tube have to be a matched set, and if the mount flange is incorrectly placed for the Fiero, then chewing gum and baling wire may be needed. ||||reg||12
Z||000002||dogtired||06-14-2000||11:53 AM||||Saw some CHROME dip-sticks and tubes at AutoZone???    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Just noticed them and didn't investigate, didn't even see what brand it was for, but thought at the time it sure would look good on my GT???    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><BR>Just what I saw    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by dogtired (edited 06-14-2000).]||||reg||6
